From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:53:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/31] MTP draft head in two stages: G6_DRAFT_HEAD2=1|2
 (default off, experimental)

kernels/head2.cuh: a 2-bit g32 screen of the rank's vocab slice (74.5 MB at TP4 instead of 134 MB INT4 / 246 MB
MXFP8, made at boot from the MXFP8 head records), the 64 best screen rows per row (deterministic histogram cut,
index order in the cut bin), their exact MXFP8 logits read out of the target's tile records, and the head record
over the 64 (log-sum-exp over the whole row, screen logits outside them); the head merge is unchanged.
Draft steps of up to 8 rows (first form, chain); wider steps keep the head GEMV. The DFlash2 head is not changed.
G6_DRAFT_HEAD2=2 also runs the MXFP8 GEMV and counts rows whose MXFP8 argmax is not a candidate (measurement).
Drafts only; in the S2 runtime signature.

runtime/tests/dhead2_test.cu (one GB10, synthetic records): conversion vs host, screen vs fp64, candidate rule vs
host, rescoring vs fp64 and the MXFP8 GEMV, head records vs k_head_local; --time: MXFP8 / INT4 / two-stage at M 1, 3, 8.
